WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.567
Cybersecurity training. Module 2. Passwords and signing in safely.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.933
A long passphrase beats a short complicated password.

3
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.933
Reuse: a password leaked from one site is tried on every other site.

4
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.533
Guessing: short or predictable passwords fall to automatic guessing.

5
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:27.600
Phishing: a fake page asks you to type it yourself.

6
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:32.133
Sharing: a person gives it away, often to someone pretending to help.

7
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.833
A text message or call is better than nothing, but easier to attack.

8
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.433
An authenticator app gives a code that changes every half minute.

9
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:49.500
A security key or passkey is the strongest: it cannot be typed into a fake page.

10
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.633
Never share a password or a code. No real support person asks for either.

11
00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:01.700
If a prompt or a code is not yours, deny it and report it.

12
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.667
Pause.

13
00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:04.900
Verify.

14
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.367
Report fast.

15
00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.500
Now read the module.
